Coding Question 1 (50 Points / Easy-Medium):Problem Description: Transaction Stream Idempotency Window Filter. Given a continuous, un-ordered stream of incoming fintech transaction payloads, each characterized by an integer transaction_id, a microsecond timestamp, and a transaction_amount, filter out duplicate processing events. A transaction is defined as a duplicate if an identical transaction_id has already been successfully registered within a strict sliding time window of W seconds. Output the total net balance processed safely without duplication.Constraints: Array/Stream size $N \le 2 \times 10^5$, transaction_id up to $10^9$, Time Window $W \le 3600$ seconds.LeetCode Canonical Mapping: Closely maps onto LC 359: Logger Rate Limiter but extended with array-based sliding window state tracking or sorting mechanics (similar to LC 933: Number of Recent Calls).

